1..20
ok 1 - precondition: both flags are on for every node and the replica's read balance is 0
ok 2 - normal following: writes reach the replica and its follower reports following
ok 3 - cut: create, update and delete on the master while the replica is unreachable; then new writes stop
ok 4 - heal: with NO new writes the replica catches up from its position — no rebuild, no pod recreation
ok 5 - ledger: the counted drop was HELD under the follower's ownership and CLOSED without a demotion
ok 6 - operator stats fetch failure: a drop whose follower cannot be probed is held as Unknown, never demoted, and closes when the probe returns
ok 7 - bulk operation: flush_all on the master advances the epoch; the follower declares needs_rebuild; the operator rebuilds it; it follows the new epoch
ok 8 - read eligibility: a following replica gets the spec's slave balance; a cut replica is withheld to 0; healing restores it
ok 9 - local read guard: stale positive balance proxies a missing value to the master while WAL remains blocked
ok 10 - repeated cuts: three cut/write/heal cycles converge from the position each time; no rebuild, no pod recreation
ok 11 - operator restart during a cut: the owned hold survives the restart; the follower catches up; the entry closes; no rebuild
ok 12 - replica crash with a backlog pending: flared killed -9 after the heal; restarts on its PVC, converges without a full dump; pod not recreated
ok 13 - planned promotion: the master pod is deleted (graceful drain); the proven follower is promoted through the gate, its epoch advances; the returning ex-master rebuilds and follows the new epoch
ok 14 - initial copy under load: a third replica joins by snapshot while writes flow, then follows and matches
ok 15 - scale: load FLARE_E2E_SCALE_KEYS keys (pipelined) and let the follower converge # SKIP FLARE_E2E_SCALE_KEYS unset (evaluation only)
ok 16 - scale: exact key scan at open (kill -9 on the PVC-backed replica) — duration recorded # SKIP FLARE_E2E_SCALE_KEYS unset (evaluation only)
ok 17 - scale: operator probe cost at this size — recorded from the operator's own timing lines # SKIP FLARE_E2E_SCALE_KEYS unset (evaluation only)
ok 18 - sustained load: does the follow stream keep up at a steady write rate, and do WAL/RSS/disk stay bounded until it does? (evaluation) # SKIP FLARE_E2E_SUSTAINED unset (evaluation only)
ok 19 - outage phase A: ~150 MB written while cut under a 256 MB WAL cap — several flushes, WAL retained; on healing the follower catches up from its cursor (no rebuild); disk/RSS high-water recorded
ok 20 - outage phase B: ~400 MB written while cut, past the 256 MB WAL cap — archived WAL purged; the follower declares needs_rebuild/lsn_purged, is rebuilt and converges; disk/RSS high-water recorded
